{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:51:46Z", "agent": "claude-edits", "seq": 22, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "## Review: Taiga #12 \u2014 Give tasks a due date\n\nRan the diff past the panel. Since the testing pass is not clean, this goes straight back to the developer per the pipeline's own rule (a blocked testing pass loops back without a review pass) \u2014 but I ran the full suite and scanned the diff first so the report is complete in one round.\n\n**Verification performed:**\n```\ncd backend && python3 -m pytest -q\n```\n\u2192 `9 failed, 38 passed`, all nine `TypeError: Object of type date is not JSON serializable` originating in `_save()`.\n\n### Will block\n\n1. **`backend/app/store.py:47`** \u2014 `_save()` still reads `json.dumps([task.model_dump() for task in self.list()])`. `model_dump()` defaults to `mode=\"python\"`, which leaves `Task.due_date` as a Python `date` object; `json.dumps` can't serialize that, so every mutation that touches a task with a due date (create-with-date, set/clear due-date, and the general persistence round-trip) throws a 500 instead of succeeding. This is exactly the blocker the developer stage flagged as denied/unapplied in its handoff \u2014 confirmed still present and still the sole cause of all 9 failures (`test_state_survives_a_simulated_restart`, `test_create_with_explicit_due_date`, `test_updating_due_date_changes_it`, `test_clearing_an_existing_due_date`, `test_updating_due_date_does_not_change_title_id_or_done`, `test_updating_due_date_with_invalid_value_is_rejected`, `test_updating_title_leaves_due_date_untouched`, `test_updating_priority_leaves_due_date_untouched`, `test_updating_due_date_leaves_priority_untouched`).\n   **Fix:** `payload = json.dumps([task.model_dump(mode=\"json\") for task in self.list()])`. Single-line change, no other edits needed \u2014 the rest of the backend/frontend diff is otherwise sound (see below).\n\n### Will comment\n\nNone.\n\n### Worth considering\n\nNone. Everything else checked out on read-through:\n- `set_due_date` in `store.py:81-87` mirrors `set_priority` exactly \u2014 consistent shape with its immediate neighbor (Stefan Ganzer lens).\n- `DueDateIn` (required key, nullable value) correctly matches the \"explicit clear\" semantics the PATCH route needs.\n- New backend tests (9 in `test_tasks.py`, 2 in `test_persistence.py`) map cleanly onto the spec's acceptance criteria, including the two cross-field \"leaves X untouched\" pairs.\n- Frontend `isOverdue` (`TaskList.jsx`) correctly implements both product defaults from the spec: strictly-before-today via ISO string comparison, and done-suppresses-overdue via `!task.done`.\n- Overdue cue uses visible text (\"Overdue\") plus a decorative `aria-hidden` icon, not colour alone \u2014 matches AC4 and the design doc's contrast notes.\n- No scope creep: frontend and backend changes both mirror the existing `priority` feature's shape one-for-one; no new surface beyond what the spec called for.\n\nThis is a one-line mechanical fix with no design or test-coverage implications \u2014 once applied, re-run `python3 -m pytest -q` and I'd expect 47/47.\n\nVERDICT: changes-requested", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Pvitm1bi88xD3mj1hedPZR", "session_id": "7d773e3f-8b00-4053-bc55-6b863de36676"}}
{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:51:46Z", "agent": "claude-edits", "seq": 23, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "## Review: Taiga #12 \u2014 Give tasks a due date (attempt 2)\n\n**Context confirmed:** the reviewer's attempt-1 blocker (`TypeError: Object of type date is not JSON serializable` in `store.py:47`) is fixed via `task.model_dump(mode=\"json\")`. I re-ran the full suite myself rather than trusting the developer's report.\n\n**Verification run this session:**\n- `cd backend && python3 -m pytest -q` \u2192 **47 passed**, 0 failures.\n- `cd frontend && npm run build` \u2192 clean build, no errors.\n- `git status --porcelain` \u2192 only the 12 expected modified files, no stray untracked files.\n\n**Diff reviewed in full:** `backend/app/{main,models,store}.py`, `backend/tests/{test_tasks,test_persistence}.py`, `frontend/src/{App.jsx,api.js}`, `frontend/src/components/{AddTask,TaskList}.jsx`, `frontend/src/App.css`, plus `docs/{spec,design}.md`.\n\n**Spec/design fidelity check (all 9 ACs):**\n- AC1/2 (optional on create) \u2014 `AddTask.jsx` defaults `dueDate=''`, maps `'' \u2192 null`, covered by `test_create_defaults_to_no_due_date`.\n- AC3 (set/change/clear from row) \u2014 `TaskList.jsx` `.due-date-input` + `.due-date-clear` button, covered by `test_clearing_an_existing_due_date`.\n- AC4 (overdue marked by more than colour) \u2014 `.overdue-badge` renders visible text \"Overdue\" plus `aria-hidden` icon; matches `docs/design.md`'s contrast computations.\n- AC5/AC6 (today and future not overdue) \u2014 `isOverdue` uses strict `<` against `todayISO()`; ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` strings compare lexicographically identically to chronological order, so this is correct without needing `Date` parsing.\n- AC7 (done suppresses badge) \u2014 `isOverdue` is gated on `!task.done`.\n- AC8 (malformed date \u2192 422) \u2014 `DueDateIn.due_date: date | None` (required key, nullable value) rejects garbage via Pydantic; covered by two dedicated tests, both passing.\n- AC9 (survives restart) \u2014 `test_due_date_absent_survives_a_simulated_restart` plus the updated existing persistence test, both passing.\n\n**Route ordering** (`main.py:48` `/due-date` before `main.py:56` generic `/{task_id}` PATCH) correctly avoids shadowing, following the same pattern as the pre-existing `/priority` route.\n\n**Store mutation pattern** (`store.py:81-87` `set_due_date`) is byte-for-byte the same shape as `set_priority`/`set_done`/`update_title` \u2014 no new idiom introduced.\n\n## Will block\nNone.\n\n## Will comment\nNone.\n\n## Worth considering\n- Frontend has no test infrastructure at all (`frontend/package.json` has no `test` script, no test files anywhere in the repo) despite `CLAUDE.md` documenting `npm test`. This is a pre-existing, project-wide gap \u2014 not introduced or worsened by this diff \u2014 and was already noted as out-of-scope in the design stage's precedent (the priority feature shipped the same way). Not this cycle's responsibility to fix.\n\nVERDICT: approve", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_0177PHBa1dP7JF6iSgLD9ySN", "session_id": "7d773e3f-8b00-4053-bc55-6b863de36676"}}
