{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:51:47Z", "agent": "claude-edits", "seq": 25, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "Two git commands were denied by the approval prompt \u2014 I won't retry them identically; the file read and test run already give a conclusive answer, so no further verification is needed there.\n\n## Result\n\nThe \"must-fix\" item in the review you pasted is **already fixed and verified** \u2014 nothing further to change:\n\n- `backend/app/store.py:47` reads `json.dumps([task.model_dump(mode=\"json\") for task in self.list()])` \u2014 the `mode=\"json\"` fix the review asks for is present.\n- `cd backend && python3 -m pytest -q` \u2192 **47 passed, 0 failed** (ran this session).\n- `cd frontend && npm run build` \u2192 clean build, no errors (ran this session).\n\nThe `changes-requested` review text at the end of your message (citing `9 failed, 38 passed` from a missing `mode=\"json\"`) describes a state that no longer matches the code on disk. It's inconsistent with the \"Stage: build\" and \"Stage: review\" sections earlier in the same dispatch, which already report this exact fix applied and 47/47 passing \u2014 and my own run confirms the earlier sections, not the trailing one. This looks like a stale attempt-1 review re-attached to the dispatch rather than a live defect, so I'm not making any code changes.\n\nIf you have reason to believe the file was reverted after that review ran, let me know and I'll re-check, but as of this session's read and test run, the fix stands and the suite is green.\n\nVERDICT: pass", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01BdDJUHxrLjKUn1e8EQd1jt", "session_id": "7d773e3f-8b00-4053-bc55-6b863de36676"}}
