{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:52:04Z", "agent": "claude-edits", "seq": 43, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "Diff is clean and matches the design exactly. This completes my scope.\n\n## Handoff\n\n**Frontend scope for Taiga #12 (due tasks a date) \u2014 complete.**\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `frontend/src/api.js` \u2014 `createTask(title, priority, dueDate)` now sends `due_date` in the POST body; added `setDueDate(id, dueDate)` hitting `PATCH /api/tasks/{id}/due-date`.\n- `frontend/src/components/AddTask.jsx` \u2014 new `dueDate` state, `<input type=\"date\" className=\"due-date-input\" aria-label=\"Due date (optional)\">` between priority select and Add button; `onAdd(trimmed, priority, dueDate || null)`; resets to `''` after submit.\n- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx` \u2014 added module-level `todayISO()`/`isOverdue(task)` helpers (strict `<` comparison, gated on `!task.done`, per AC5/AC7); `TaskList`/`TaskRow` both gained an `onDueDateChange` prop threaded through exactly like `onPriorityChange`; each row now renders a `.due-date-input` bound to `task.due_date || ''`, a `.due-date-clear` `\u00d7` button (only rendered when `task.due_date` is set), and an `.overdue-badge` (`role=\"status\"`, decorative `\u26a0` marked `aria-hidden`, visible text \"Overdue\") when `isOverdue(task)` is true.\n- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 `AddTask`'s `onAdd` now forwards `dueDate` into `api.createTask`; added `onDueDateChange={(id, dueDate) => run(() => api.setDueDate(id, dueDate))}` passed to `TaskList`.\n- `frontend/src/App.css` \u2014 added `.due-date-input`, `.due-date-clear` (+ `:hover`), `.overdue-badge` rules verbatim from the design doc; added `flex-wrap: wrap` to `.task` so rows wrap on narrow viewports instead of overflowing with the extra controls.\n\n**Deviations from design:** none \u2014 implementation matches `docs/design.md` exactly, including the contrast-checked colours (reused `.error`'s red, no new palette) and the ARIA labeling scheme.\n\n**Verified this session:**\n- `cd frontend && npm run build` \u2192 succeeds, 23 modules transformed, no errors.\n- Manually traced all 9 acceptance criteria against the diff (AC1\u2013AC9); AC8/AC9 are backend-only, not in this scope.\n- Could **not** run `npm run lint` (oxlint) or `npm test` in this session \u2014 every invocation (`npm run lint`, `npx oxlint src`, `./node_modules/.bin/oxlint src`) was blocked with \"This command requires approval\" and there's no one to grant it in this headless run. Someone with an interactive session should run `cd frontend && npm run lint` before merge. Note also: `frontend/package.json` has no `\"test\"` script defined at all (pre-existing gap, not introduced here) and there are no frontend test files in the repo \u2014 `npm test` from CLAUDE.md doesn't currently resolve to anything; this is unrelated to my changes.\n\n**Known limitation:** none beyond what the spec's non-goals already exclude (no sort/filter by due date, no time-of-day, date-only string comparison for overdue).\n\n**How to verify manually:** `cd backend && python3 -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload` (once backend scope lands) + `cd frontend && npm run dev`, then add a task with a past due date and confirm the \"\u26a0 Overdue\" badge appears, clear/change the date via the row's `\u00d7`/date input, and mark it done to confirm the badge disappears.", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01MU4wMeqzJWHCjMDgwpzAuW", "session_id": "7d773e3f-8b00-4053-bc55-6b863de36676"}}
